# Deepcore — Controls

This file defines the actions the game is driven by, the keys bound to them, and
what each does on each screen. Every action name and key below carries the name
this specification gives it.

{{#if (eq engine.slug "none")}}
Keyboard input belongs to the runtime layer you write. It reads
`KeyboardEvent.code`, so the bindings are layout-independent, and it reports for
each action whether it is held now and whether it went down this frame. The mouse
belongs to that layer too, reporting the pointer's position in the stage's logical
units along with its press and release.
{{else if (eq engine.slug "simple-2d")}}
Input belongs to the {{engine.name}} engine. The game registers each action below
by name against the codes bound to it, and the engine reports whether the action
is held and whether it went down this frame. Actions are read anywhere in the
game's update. The engine also reports the pointer's position in the stage's
logical units along with its press and release edges.
{{else}}
Input belongs to the {{engine.name}} engine. The game registers each action below
by name against the codes bound to it, and the engine reports whether the action
is held and whether it went down this frame. Actions are read inside the player
controller alone. The engine also hands the game the pointer's ordered samples in
the stage's logical units, with its press and release edges.
{{/if}}

## The actions

`ACTIONS` binds each action name to the `KeyboardEvent.code` values that drive it.

| Action | Codes |
| --- | --- |
| `left` | `KeyA`, `ArrowLeft` |
| `right` | `KeyD`, `ArrowRight` |
| `down` | `KeyS`, `ArrowDown` |
| `up` | `KeyW`, `ArrowUp`, `Space` |
| `activate` | `KeyE`, `Enter` |
| `inventory` | `KeyI` |
| `pause` | `Escape` |
| `mute` | `KeyM` |
| `jettison` | `KeyJ` |
| `supply1` through `supply6` | `Digit1` through `Digit6` |

## In the mine

Movement is continuous: an action drives the miner for as long as it is held.

| Action | Effect |
| --- | --- |
| `left`, `right` | Walk that way. Once the miner's box is flush against a minable cell on that side and the miner is grounded, cut into it and then move into the tunnel it leaves. |
| `down` | While grounded, cut the cell below and sink into it. With open space below, nothing; the miner simply falls. |
| `up` | Fire the jetpack. |
| `activate` | At a surface building, open its panel, or save at the Save Pad. |
| `inventory` | Open and close the inventory overlay. |
| `pause` | Open the pause menu, or close an open panel. |
| `mute` | Toggle all audio. |
| `jettison` | Drop a carried Core Sample onto the miner's cell. |
| `supply1` through `supply6` | Use the field supply of that number. |

The miner faces the direction of the last `left` or `right` held, and its sprite
mirrors to match.

## On a menu screen

| Action | Effect |
| --- | --- |
| `up`, `down` | Move the highlighted item up and down, wrapping at the ends. |
| `activate` | Choose the highlighted item. |
| `pause` | Go back, where the screen has a back. |

## With the mouse

Every menu item, panel control, and status-bar control is clickable. Clicking a
surface building activates it, exactly as `activate` does while standing at it.
The first-time hazard notice card is dismissed by a click on it.

A control is drawn as operable only where it acts. Where the game cannot act on a
control in the state it is in, that control is drawn disabled or is not drawn at
all, and it neither highlights under the pointer nor answers a click.

The game is fully playable with the keyboard for movement, drilling, and thrust,
and the mouse for the panels and menus. No control beyond those listed here is
required.
